  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array BBB containing NNN integers, each of which is either −1-1−1 or a non-negative integer. Construct **any** integer array AAA of length NNN such that:\n\n\n0≤Ai≤1090 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^90≤Ai​≤109 for every 1≤i≤N1 \\leq i \\leq N1≤i≤N\nIf Bi≥0B_i \\geq 0Bi​≥0, AAA must satisfy mex(A1,A2,…,Ai)=Bimex(A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_i) = B_imex(A1​,A2​,…,Ai​)=Bi​\nOtherwise, Bi=−1B_i = -1Bi​=−1, which means there is no constraint on mex(A1,A2,…,Ai)mex(A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_i)mex(A1​,A2​,…,Ai​)\nIf there does not exist any array satisfying the constraints, print −1-1−1 instead.\n\n**Note:** The mex of a set of non-negative integers is the smallest non-negative integer that does not belong to it. For example, mex(1,2,3)=0,mex(0,2,4,1)=3,mex(1, 2, 3) = 0, mex(0, 2, 4, 1) = 3,mex(1,2,3)=0,mex(0,2,4,1)=3, and mex(0,0,0)=1mex(0, 0, 0) = 1mex(0,0,0)=1.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains an integer TTT, denoting the number of testcases. The description of TTT testcases follows.\nThe first line of each testcase contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line of each testcase contains NNN space-separated integers B1,B2,…,BNB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_NB1​,B2​,…,BN​.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each testcase, output the required answer on a new line: −1-1−1 if no valid array exists, or NNN space-separated integers denoting the elements of **any** valid array AAA. The elements of AAA must satisfy 0≤Ai≤1090 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^90≤Ai​≤109.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "−1≤Bi≤105-1 \\leq B_i \\leq 10^5−1≤Bi​≤105",
      "The sum of NNN across all testcases won't exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n7\n0 -1 2 -1 5 -1 -1\n3\n2 -1 -1",
        "output": "1 3 0 4 2 6 5\n-1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: We have A=[1,3,0,4,2,6,5]A = [1, 3, 0, 4, 2, 6, 5]A=[1,3,0,4,2,6,5]. Let Ci=mex(A1,A2,…,Ai)C_i = mex(A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_i)Ci​=mex(A1​,A2​,…,Ai​). Then, it can be seen that C=[0,0,2,2,5,5,7]C = [0, 0, 2, 2, 5, 5, 7]C=[0,0,2,2,5,5,7], which matches BBB at all positions where Bi≥0B_i \\geq 0Bi​≥0.\nTest case 222: It can be shown that no array AAA exists that satisfies the given constraints."
      }
    ]
